// Bitcoin Script Example: Arithmetic Operations
//
// Transaction version: 2
// It keeps every intermediate value on the stack to show the steps, and
// version 1 requires exactly one item at the end.
//
// This script demonstrates basic arithmetic opcodes

// Simple addition
5 10 add
// Stack: [15]

// Duplicate and add to itself
dup add
// Stack: [30]

// More complex arithmetic
100 50 sub
// Stack: [30, 50]

2 mul
// Stack: [30, 100]

// Division and modulo
25 5 div
// Stack: [30, 100, 5]

20 7 mod
// Stack: [30, 100, 5, 6]

// Min and max operations
100 200 max
// Stack: [30, 100, 5, 6, 200]

50 25 min
// Stack: [30, 100, 5, 6, 200, 25]

// Within check: is 100 within [50, 150)?
100 50 150 within
// Stack: [30, 100, 5, 6, 200, 25, 1]

// Final stack will show all intermediate results
